images.caption:
Portsmouth, North Carolina an abandoned village on North Core Banks: Lionel &amp; Emma Gilgo House built circa 1926 by Roy Robinson on Coast Guard property at the site of the Marine Hospital[1].
Residents

1926 Roy Robinson and family;
1931 Coast Guardsmen;
1938 house moved for Lionel Gilgo, and Emma Hunnings  Gilgo and children;
1942 the family moved from Portsmouth when school closed.
This house is under a Private Lease.

