images.caption:
Portsmouth, North Carolina an abandoned village on North Core Banks: Walker &amp; Sarah Styron House built by Robert Wallace in circa 1850. The original kitchen was destroyed by a hurricane in the 1920’s[1].
Residents: 

1837 Robert Wallace and family;
1882 John and Theresa Grace and two sons;
1911 Amanda Jane Dixon;
1927 Sarah Roberts Styron and Coast Guardsman Walker Styron and one daughter;
1949 Joffre L. and Lillian M. Coe.

