Portsmouth, North Carolina an abandoned village on North Core Banks: Washington Roberts House built by Zacharrah Styron in circa 1840, this is the oldest house surviving in Portsmouth Village, nicknamed the “Hurricane House”[1].
Residents

1849 David Ireland;
1889 Washington Roberts, mother, and 2 sisters;
1930 Joe Abbot

